From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:04:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 42/48] net: airoha: xpon: use the stock T-CONT reset image
 only on EN751221

The 0x00ff00ff image written to the T-CONT pair registers on session
stop comes from the stock EN751221 gponDevResetAllocId(). Use it only
there; on EN7523/EN7528 write TCONT_PAIR_INVALID, which clears the
valid bits just as __gpon_set_tcont_hw() already does for one entry.
The PLOAMd filter and the stock AES sequence were limited to EN751221
in their own fixes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
index 6c4e8bf..229bbf4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -3597,10 +3597,16 @@ static void gpon_clear_hw_tables(struct xpon_priv *priv)
 	}
 
 	if (READ_ONCE(gpon_stop_clear_tconts)) {
+		/* The reset image is the stock EN751221 one; elsewhere just
+		 * clear the valid bits.
+		 */
+		u32 image = gpon_stock_en751221_csr(priv) ?
+			    GPON_TCONT_PAIR_RESET : TCONT_PAIR_INVALID;
+
 		mutex_lock(&priv->tcont_lock);
 		for (reg = GPON_TCONT_ID_0_1; reg <= GPON_TCONT_ID_14_15;
 		     reg += 4)
-			gpon_write(priv, reg, GPON_TCONT_PAIR_RESET);
+			gpon_write(priv, reg, image);
 		for (index = 16; index < GPON_MAX_TCONT; index++)
 			if (priv->tcont_alloc_id[index] !=
 			    GPON_TCONT_UNASSIGNED &&
